# The media site on the dev stack (book P2.19; ADR 0029, ADR 0070 point 5): staging.usercontent.unset.site, the
# media process's draft previews, through Pangolin and Newt like the other dev sites (ADR 0030 Decision 2, ADR 0032 Decision 5), so it
# binds the newt_edge address only, serves the dev leaf, and is never indexed. Its name and upstream are ruled values
# (adapted-rules.ts DEV_MEDIA). The media process sets its own sandbox CSP and nosniff on every answer and refuses
# every method but GET and HEAD; the edge adds the security headers and drops the client's address before media, as on
# every site. The access log already drops the request URI (snippets/log.caddy), so no signed link's sig is logged.
# One read-only file bind at /etc/caddy/sites/enabled/media.caddy (compose.dev.yaml, compose.dev.source.yaml).
{$MEDIA_HOST} {
	bind 10.250.37.3
	import tls
	import access-log
	import security-headers
	import too-many-tries
	import noindex
	route {
		# One zone, every request, keyed on the client (limits.json mediaRateLimitZones; limits.budget.test.ts), so one
		# address cannot slow previews for every tester (ADR 0029). An editor page with twelve pictures in three sizes
		# is 36 requests; a member reloading it every three seconds for five minutes is 3,600.
		rate_limit {
			zone media_global {
				key {client_ip}
				ipv6_prefix 64
				events 6000
				window 5m
			}
			disable_metrics
		}
		import upstream {$MEDIA_UPSTREAM}
	}
}
